ompensation of $757 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Krispy Kreme, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $547M market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $64M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 46% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 700% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 38% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 66% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6585243264977882},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Large open-market insider purchases (net $3.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Krispy Kreme (NASDAQ:DNUT) Shares Down 7.5% \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/17/krispy-kreme-nasdaqdnut-shares-down-7-5-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794947600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Krispy Kreme (NASDAQ:DNUT) Price Target Raised to $4.80","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/krispy-kreme-nasdaqdnut-price-target-raised-to-4-80.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794468289.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Understanding Krispy Kreme (DNUT) Reliance on International Revenue","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028147/understanding-krispy-kreme-dnut-reliance-on-international-revenue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_international_revenues-3028147","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428623.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"compa